{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527073-the-renegade-studios-adventures-thread","id":1527073,"title":"The Renegade Studios adventures thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-18T16:53:38-08:00","id":1527073,"title":"The Renegade Studios adventures thread","content":"I think the absolute height of V5 will end up being the OPP work and the best Renegade Studios books are going to be ending up the ones they're reprinting. I hope OPP got a good deal for that because Chicago by Night, Cults of the Blood Gods, and (not OPP) The Fall of London are all excellent books. However, that doesn't mean I don't think there's some decent stuff that they've churned out.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the stuff I like the most is their adventures.<br /> <br /> Love Bites: A Vampire: The Masquerade New Years Eve Story (Free)<br /> <br /> A Taste of the Moon<br /> <br /> Last Dance at Renaulds<br /> <br /> Midnight Kiss: A Vampire: The Masquerade New Year's Eve Story (Free)<br /> <br /> Auld Sanguine: A Vampire: The Masquerade New Year's Eye Story (Free)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 12-30-2023, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T10:51:46-08:00","id":1527632,"title":"","content":"Fall of London is more an aquired taste myself and I use it as fleshing the backgrounds of any other player characters that I might have hailed from there. The rest of the titles are quite good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T11:14:13-08:00","id":1527637,"title":"","content":"As Lysander said Fall of London is a fair way down the ladder from the other two in my books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T12:28:14-08:00","id":1527638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527073-the-renegade-studios-adventures-thread?p=1527632#post1527632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fall of London is more an aquired taste myself and I use it as fleshing the backgrounds of any other player characters that I might have hailed from there. The rest of the titles are quite good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say Fall of London would qualify as it's a reprint.<br /> <br /> Nor would Let the Streets Run Red or Trails of Ashes and Bone.<br /> <br /> These were actually referring to the Renegade published adventures. Which are available on their website in PDF form.<br /> <br /> I noticed no one was talking about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T22:15:30-08:00","id":1529802,"title":"","content":"<b>Midnight Kiss</b><br /> <br /> <b>Summary</b>: The player characters are invited to a Nephilim party in their home city. They are subjected to a number of temptations and cruel tests by the sadistic collection of beauty-worshiping assholes. This is actually an attempt by the cult's leader to solidify his position after mounting a coup against the previous one. Oh and there's some Second Inquisition operatives involved too, though they only want to get their missing (and brainwashed) friend.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I never had any interest in <i>Constantinople by Night</i> but the writers of <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i> did a fantastic job of making them relevant to the modern nights. I felt the diablerie by Mary the Black of Michael as well as the set up of the New Trinity was something that was really interesting. I've often struggled for ways to incorporate the Baali into campaigns because, well, they're really just too dark as well as seeming lacking in subtlety.<br /> <br /> The Baali seemingly vanished from the setting with V5, perhaps for the desire to avoid controversy, but I strangely think the Nephilim are the perfect group to reintroduce them. Given I think the OPP people are geniuses, I believe they inserted the Nephilim as a way to use the Baali and Mary the Black's plot without implicitly stating they're puppest for the Unholy. The Nephilim worhip beauty but are twisted and sadistic, reveling in their loss of humanity as well as idolatrous worship of Michael.<br /> <br /> I also like the use of Hunters because these hunters hate Kindred but their leader just wants to save their friend. Unfortunately, that may be imposible because their friend has had their brain fried by too much pleasure. They're ghouled, sexed up, and absolutely of the mind the Kindred are awesome now. It leads to some very interesting possibilities here. Also, the other two hunters would gladly like to see you all killed but may be persuaded if they don't see you engaged in horrifying atrocities like most of the &quot;guests&quot; here tonight.<br /> <br /> Plus, as always, Elders vs. childer.<br /> <br /> A solid effort and I wish this would have been released in a physical book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:01:42-08:00","id":1530291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527073-the-renegade-studios-adventures-thread?p=1529802#post1529802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Midnight Kiss</b><br /> <br /> <b>Summary</b>: The player characters are invited to a Nephilim party in their home city. They are subjected to a number of temptations and cruel tests by the sadistic collection of beauty-worshiping assholes. This is actually an attempt by the cult's leader to solidify his position after mounting a coup against the previous one. Oh and there's some Second Inquisition operatives involved too, though they only want to get their missing (and brainwashed) friend.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I never had any interest in <i>Constantinople by Night</i> but the writers of <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i> did a fantastic job of making them relevant to the modern nights. I felt the diablerie by Mary the Black of Michael as well as the set up of the New Trinity was something that was really interesting. I've often struggled for ways to incorporate the Baali into campaigns because, well, they're really just too dark as well as seeming lacking in subtlety.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a die-hard fan of Costantinople by Night, I very much looked forward to the <b>Nephilim</b> and to <b>Midnight Kiss </b>for the reasons you presented here. Unfortunately, I feel their writeup both in <i>Cults fo the Blood Gods</i> and in the adventure is a bit too much focused on Beauty, I think it risks of projecting them as &quot;<i>snotty Toreador on steroids</i>&quot;. Which is a pity because the adventure is really good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}